    "multi_column_R8Nq8b": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "column_tFjTG4": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/scott_kremp.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Scott Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>President</strong></p><p>Scott grew up in the family business then joined full time after attending Gettysburg College (’87).  Graduating with a degree in business management, he learned all facets of the flower business while participating in<br/>many industry activities.  In his free time, Scott enjoys all sports, and spending time with his family.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_TC3MqU": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_2879.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Steve Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>VP Greenhouse Operations</strong></p><p>Steve graduated from Saint Lawrence University('89) in upstate New York with a Bachelor of science degree in Biology with a heavy emphasis on ecology.   His work experience has ranged from bagging fish at Martin's aquarium and restoring dioramas at the Academy of Natural Sciences, to commercial salmon fishing in Alaska and overseeing wildlife conservation projects.   He managed several Kremp florist retail locations in Philadelphia and the surrounding area before shifting his focus to horticulture.  He gained first hand growing experience at Fetzer greenhouses then moved to Bucks county, with his wife Leslie and two children, where his vision of Kremp Florist's own production facility came to life.   He has focused on growing the highest quality cut flowers, poinsettias, annuals and hanging baskets, as well as hundreds of varieties of figs from around the world.  When not tending to the crops, he enjoys seeking solitude and adventure in the world's remaining wild places.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_6W6qC9": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/KSQUARE.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Drew Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>VP Retail Sales/Maintenance</strong></p><p>Drew started in the flower business at an early age coming to work with his father to help design funeral arrangements on the weekends.  Graduating from New England College (’91), he promptly started full time.  He loves to come to work each day working with his brothers and wears many hats throughout the building.  Away from work, Drew's hobbies include flying his airplane, fishing, yard work and odd jobs around the house. </p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_kxjULU": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Chad-Kremp-264x300.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Chad Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>VP Sales & Technology</strong></p><p>After graduating from Ithaca College('97) with a degree in marketing and advertising, Chad joined the family business just as the internet was taking off.  At a time when websites were simple static pages, Chad embraced the opportunity to grow the Kremp online presence and ecommerce platform.  While overseeing all sales activities and our customer service team, Chad sources many of the unique gift items Kremp sells. In his free time, Chad enjoys family time, is a musician and loves hearing from the many Goldbergs fans out there!</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_UYf4ha": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_5105.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Leslie Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>Special Event/Sales Manager</strong></p><p>Leslie grew up around the flower business spending many childhood Saturdays helping out at her grandmother's flower shop in NE Philly. After marrying her Jenkintown HS ('84, Blue) Junior Prom date- Steve Kremp- Leslie moved on from her career in advertising to join the Kremp family business. A proud mom of two grown children, when she's not helping brides to design the wedding flowers of their dreams, you'll find her in her kitchen maybe making pasta, maybe making soup, maybe making bread -- but always cooking with most likely Louis Prima radio as the soundtrack! </p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_i93PTA": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "enable_media": true,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/KSQUARE.jpg",
            "media_scale": 100,
            "heading": "Charles Kremp",
            "heading_link": "",
            "text": "<p><strong>Chairman</strong></p><p>Charles  is 1 of 13 retail florist owners to be named to the <a href=\"https://safnow.org/about-saf/awards-certifications/hall-of-fame-2/\" title=\"https://safnow.org/about-saf/awards-certifications/hall-of-fame-2/\">Society of American Florists Floriculture Hall of Fame</a>.  He has also been named Pennsylvania Florist of the Year, Citizen of the Year by the local chamber of commerce and honored with many other notable industry awards.  He assists with long-term planning, finances and is a staple at our stand at the Philadelphia Flower Show each year.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        }
      },
